API-01: shift tank rule premises before counting the new junction

EN_addnode calls adjusttankrules() after it has incremented Njuncs.
adjusttankrules() shifts premises whose node index is greater than
Njuncs, so the premise on the first tank or reservoir (index old
Njuncs + 1) is not shifted and ends up on the new junction. The call
now comes before Njuncs is incremented, while every tank and
reservoir index is still greater than Njuncs.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-01_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..52e1349 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -1963,6 +1963,10 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_addnode(EN_Project p, const char *id, int nodeType, int *index)
             net->Node[i + 1] = net->Node[i];
         }
 
+        // adjust indices of tanks/reservoirs in Rule premises (see RULES.C)
+        // (before Njuncs is incremented, since it shifts indices > Njuncs)
+        adjusttankrules(p, 1);
+
         // set index of new Junction node
         net->Njuncs++;
         nIdx = net->Njuncs;
@@ -1987,8 +1991,6 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_addnode(EN_Project p, const char *id, int nodeType, int *index)
             control = &net->Control[i];
             if (control->Node > net->Njuncs - 1) control->Node += 1;
         }
-        // adjust indices of tanks/reservoirs in Rule premises (see RULES.C)
-        adjusttankrules(p, 1);
     }
 
     // Actions taken when a new Tank/Reservoir is added
